<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jean Decoux</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1884">1884</a>–<a href="/years/1963">1963</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Admiral Jean Decoux</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jean Decoux was a French admiral who governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indochina">French Indochina</a> for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vichy">Vichy</a> regime from 1940 to 1945. He accepted the stationing of Japanese troops in the colony while keeping French administration in place, and promoted youth, sports and local patriotic movements loyal to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippe-petain">Marshal Pétain</a>. He was removed when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> seized power in March 1945 and was later tried in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jean-decoux.jpg" alt="Jean Decoux" width="262" height="285" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Remerciements Jacques Decoux · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jean_Decoux_1919.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>During the Second World War <b>Admiral Jean Decoux</b> governed for Vichy France from 1940 to 1945, promoting youth and sports movements and local patriotism loyal to Marshal Pétain while sharing the colony with Japanese forces.</blockquote><a href="/empire/french-indochina">French Indochina · Governance &amp; Law</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Bordeaux, in what is now <a href="/countries/france">France</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/france">France</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=44.84,-0.58&amp;year=1935" aria-label="Bordeaux on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4536 579 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Jean Decoux"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4986 849h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4986 849h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=44.84,-0.58&amp;year=1935">What was here in 1935? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
